  "recipes": {
    "raw-bound": "Suite/bundle: UTF-8 quoted literal é surrounded by spaces to exact bound+delta. Artifact: quoted repeated literal backslash-u00e9, ASCII a remainder, and one escaped quote; original token exactly 1MiB+delta. Canonical expectation built from literal é repetitions plus a and escaped quote, not serializer output. Separate artifact internal-whitespace at/over rows use [ then padding then 0], literal canonical [0]. Outside-token whitespace never contributes to token span.",
    "aggregate": "One synthetic accounting object at a time, not a Suite/Bundle schema: artifacts of at most 1MiB-2 decoded units (text) or 1MiB canonical bytes (JSON strings), plus remainder, total exactly 20MiB+delta. Raw tokens <=1MiB. Literal repeated a contents, same id index in each independent array. Expect totals before aggregate rejection; then separately impose suite/embedded 5MiB or containing bundle 25MiB raw limit and component result. Embedded suite checks include both suite and bundle limits; component pass never implies envelope fit.",
    "depth": "opening repeated depth, quoted leaf [ {} ] with an escaped quote, closing repeated depth; independently construct identical canonical bytes without whitespace. Primitive/root type controls also exercised by N2.",
    "roles": "Six replacement-N2 token rows each check root and repeated token at /content/nested/0, /expected, /actual, /subject, /integer, plus an unchanged text representation and null control. Literal key-sorted canonical template substitutes manifest canon. Types/scalar/integer gates checked pre/post-reparse; required non-Scalar expected/subject returns E_SCHEMA, wrong actual against integer 1 reports only type-compatible=false, never evaluator result. Exact type+value comparison distinguishes bool. Compare canonical hash to independently specified bytes; raw hash may differ. Legacy P39/P40 retain null/string Scalar controls unchanged."
  }
